ety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Password selection appears in “Organizational Security”. Define its role and features, relate it to Piggybacking, Shoulder surfing, Dumpster diving, Installing unauthorized software, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Piggybacking, Shoulder surfing, Dumpster diving, Installing unauthorized software, hardware. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Cyber Security task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Overview of IP Security (IPSec) appears in “IP Security”. Define its role and features, relate it to IP Security Architecture, Modes of Operation, Security Associations (SA) Security Parameter Index (SPI), SA Management, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to IP Security Architecture, Modes of Operation, Security Associations (SA) Security Parameter Index (SPI), SA Management, Security Policy. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete