VALUES (4900932006110129, ARRAY['"[8 marks] A practical problem in Fundamental of Data Mining involves the syllabus topic data mining concepts as applied within Data Mining and Data Processing. Explain how Data mining concepts applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Fundamental of Data Mining involves the syllabus topic association rules as applied within Data Mining Techniques. Explain how Association rules applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Fundamental of Data Mining involves the syllabus topic cluster analysis as applied within Clustering Methods. Explain how Cluster analysis applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Fundamental of Data Mining involves the syllabus topic data mining applications as applied within Applications of Data Mining. Explain how Data mining applications applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Data mining concepts appears in “Data Mining and Data Processing”. Define its role and features, relate it to data processing, data preprocessing, data processing systems, data preparation, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to data processing, data preprocessing, data processing systems, data preparation, data quality. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Fundamental of Data Mining task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Association rules appears in “Data Mining Techniques”. Define its role and features, relate it to classification, regression, clustering, neural networks, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to classification, regression, clustering, neural networks, predictive modeling. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Fundamental of Data Mining task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Cluster analysis appears in “Clustering Methods”. Define its role and features, relate it to K means clustering, hierarchical clustering, agglomerative clustering, divisive clustering, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to K means clustering, hierarchical clustering, agglomerative clustering, divisive clustering, cluster evaluation. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Fundamental of Data Mining task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Data mining applications appears in “Applications of Data Mining”. Define its role and features, relate it to business applications, risk management, targeted marketing, customer profiles, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to business applications, risk management, targeted marketing, customer profiles, prediction. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Fundamental of Data Mining task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

