VALUES (4900932006010129, ARRAY['"[8 marks] A practical problem in Management Information System involves the syllabus topic information systems and their roles as applied within Information Systems and MIS Fundamentals. Explain how Information systems and their roles applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Management Information System involves the syllabus topic systems analysts as applied within MIS Development and Design. Explain how Systems analysts applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Management Information System involves the syllabus topic decision support systems dss as applied within Decision Support Systems and Business Intelligence. Explain how Decision support systems DSS applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Management Information System involves the syllabus topic challenges of managing it functions as applied within Managing the IT Function. Explain how Challenges of managing IT functions applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Information systems and their roles appears in “Information Systems and MIS Fundamentals”. Define its role and features, relate it to classify information, management information systems, benefits of MIS, limitations of MIS, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to classify information, management information systems, benefits of MIS, limitations of MIS, Information Systems and MIS Fundamentals. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Management Information System task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Systems analysts appears in “MIS Development and Design”. Define its role and features, relate it to tools used by system analysts, MIS development life cycle, MIS development models, MIS design, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to tools used by system analysts, MIS development life cycle, MIS development models, MIS design, MIS Development and Design. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Management Information System task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Decision support systems DSS appears in “Decision Support Systems and Business Intelligence”. Define its role and features, relate it to management and decision making, types of decisions, analytics, business intelligence, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to management and decision making, types of decisions, analytics, business intelligence, BI techniques. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Management Information System task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Challenges of managing IT functions appears in “Managing the IT Function”. Define its role and features, relate it to modern IT environment, centralization, decentralization, IT security, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to modern IT environment, centralization, decentralization, IT security, technology selection. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Management Information System task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

