. Define its role and features, relate it to reflection and transmission coefficient, standing wave and standing wave ratio, line impedance and admittance, impedance matching, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to reflection and transmission coefficient, standing wave and standing wave ratio, line impedance and admittance, impedance matching, using stub line. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete RF and Microwave Communication task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Equivalent voltages and currents for non-TEM lines appears in “Microwave Network Analysis”. Define its role and features, relate it to Network parameters for microwave circuits, Scattering Parameters, Microwave Network Analysis, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Network parameters for microwave circuits, Scattering Parameters, Microwave Network Analysis. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete RF and Microwave Communication task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

