VALUES (4900932006090129, ARRAY['"[8 marks] A practical problem in Wireless Technologies involves the syllabus topic cellular cell concepts: cell structure as applied within Introduction to Cellular Communication. Explain how Cellular cell concepts: cell structure applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Wireless Technologies involves the syllabus topic services and features as applied within Global System for Mobile Communications (GSM). Explain how Services and Features applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Wireless Technologies involves the syllabus topic architecture of is-95 cdma system as applied within CDMA. Explain how Architecture of IS-95 CDMA system applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Wireless Technologies involves the syllabus topic stack as applied within Wireless Personal Area Networks: Bluetooth Specifications, Protocols. Explain how Stack applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Cellular cell concepts: cell structure appears in “Introduction to Cellular Communication”. Define its role and features, relate it to frequency reuse, cell splitting, cell sectoring, Microcell zone concept, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to frequency reuse, cell splitting, cell sectoring, Microcell zone concept, channel assignment. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Wireless Technologies task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Services and Features appears in “Global System for Mobile Communications (GSM)”. Define its role and features, relate it to System Architecture, Radio sub systems, Channel types, Example of a GSM call, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to System Architecture, Radio sub systems, Channel types, Example of a GSM call, Frame Structure. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Wireless Technologies task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Architecture of IS-95 CDMA system appears in “CDMA”. Define its role and features, relate it to CDMA forward channels, CDMA reverse channels, Soft handoff, CDMA features, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to CDMA forward channels, CDMA reverse channels, Soft handoff, CDMA features, Power control in CDMA. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Wireless Technologies task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Stack appears in “Wireless Personal Area Networks: Bluetooth Specifications, Protocols”. Define its role and features, relate it to Security Issues, Advantages and Disadvantages, Application, UWB, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Security Issues, Advantages and Disadvantages, Application, UWB, Zigbee. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Wireless Technologies task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);
